2186362318 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e1d8d74b-55cf-51de-803f-0cecc60a4fb1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362318 #edb/ref 1074 "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nThe phase line that corresponds to the given graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/36/362ffe8871efa8dc597708b039fa766c3603777ba12460e84d9af1fc39800288.png)\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n- Statement I is true. From the phase line, we see that $y=-3$ is a node.\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. From the phase line, we see that $y=2$ is a sink.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363419 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363420 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363419 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363421 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363419 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363422 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363419 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363423 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363419 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363424 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363419 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363419 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363419 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186363424 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363419 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "669d7279-38d4-5150-94a0-6a97a679c0f2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363420 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{n\\pi }{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363420 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363420 #edb